    "author": "Bordone, M., Khodjamirian, A., and Mannel, T.",
    "title": "New Sum Rules for the $B_c \\to J/\\psi$ Form Factors",
    "abstract": "We derive new sum rules for the form factors of the $B_c\\to J/\\psi\\, \\ell \\bar{\\nu}_\\ell$ semileptonic transitions, employing the vacuum-to-$B_c$ correlation function of the $J/\\psi$-interpolating and $b\\to c$ weak currents. In the heavy quark limit and at a space-like momentum transfer to the weak current, a local operator-product expansion is valid for this correlation function. As a result, in the leading power, the non-perturbative input is reduced to the decay constant of $B_c$ meson. Furthermore, applying hadronic dispersion relation in the $J/\\psi$ channel, we find that a non-vanishing OPE spectral density in the duality interval of $J/\\psi$ emerges only at $\\mathcal{O}(\\alpha_s)$. We calculate this density in the relevant kinematic regime. The $B_c\\to J/\\psi$ form factors at space-like momentum transfer are then calculated from the new sum rules.",
